image — must carry this notice in its accompanying materials (see ../../THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES).

DERIVED, AND MODIFIED. Diffed against golang.org/x/exp/mmap@v0.0.0-20260727155853:

  mmap_unix.go     upstream, plus a Bytes() accessor on ReaderAt
  mmap_windows.go  upstream, plus the same Bytes() accessor
  mmap_other.go    substantially rewritten -- the fallback reads the whole file into
                   memory at Open so the Bytes() API holds on platforms with no mmap
                   binding here, where upstream reads through the *os.File instead
  mmap_test.go     extended (34 -> 101 lines)

NOT DERIVED. These are original netstar-labs work and are not covered by the license
below; upstream x/exp/mmap is read-only (ReaderAt) and has no writable mapping at all:

  rw.go            the RW type -- a writable MAP_SHARED mapping
  rw_unix.go       MapRW, Sync, SyncRange on linux/darwin
  rw_other.go      the non-file-backed fallback

